    isbefore: []  # d6f8
    duplicate_of: []  # d6f8
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d6f8
    pr_ref:  # d6f8
    description: "All 11 kind=main_function entrypoints share one kind, but their target node.kind splits: 9 -> function (label 'Python main()'), 2 -> file (label 'Python script (if __name__ == 0x27__main__0x27)', id __main__.py:1-1:file:file, confidence 1.0). The spec example ('main_function','main') at line 351 implies a function target; the file-target case is undocumented. A consumer keying on kind=main_function to jump to a callable entrypoint must handle BOTH a function and a file target; confidence (1.0 on both) doesn't disambiguate, only the free-text label does. Fresh-run reproduced: a temp pkg/__main__.py containing if __name__=='__main__' and NO main() function yields main_function EP conf=0.96 label='Python script (if __name__...)' target_kind=file id=python:pkg/__main__.py:1-1:file:file; the converse (a file with def main()) points to the function node. So the file-target is a real, reproducible detector behavior, not an artifact. Secondary: spec §890/§643 says if __name__=='__main__' is 0.85 Structural confidence but substrate + fresh run show 1.0/0.96 (confidence drift, likely within WI-suvil hardcoded-confidence family; not separately filed)."  # d6f8
    fields: {}  # d6f8
