  message: "Done in PR #359 (ff-merged to dev). Behavioral item; re-ran the item's own filed repro with the EDITABLE install (.venv/bin/hypergumbo).\n\nBEFORE: kind=main_function overloaded — a guard-only __main__.py (no def main()) and a def main() BOTH emitted kind=main_function (targets file vs function respectively, conf 1.0), disambiguated only by the free-text label.\nAFTER (editable-binary repro):\n- /tmp/tuv_guard (__main__.py: 'if __name__' guard, NO main()) -> kind=main_guard target_kind=file label='Python script (if __name__ == ...)'.\n- /tmp/tuv_func (def main() + 'if __name__: main()') -> single kind=main_function target_kind=function label='Python main()' (guard deduped — INV-hosuh preserved).\nSo kind ALONE now disambiguates the target type (main_function->function, main_guard->file).\n\nImplementation: new EntrypointKind.MAIN_GUARD (auto-registered into the entrypoint-kind catalog axis + generated Entrypoint.kind schema enum); main_guard concept emits it; INV-hosuh post-pass updated to supersede same-path MAIN_GUARD with a function-target MAIN_FUNCTION. Ripples (behavior-preserving): sketch _ENTRYPOINT_GROUPS 'CLI & Scripts' + cli _MAIN_KINDS slice boost include MAIN_GUARD; dead-code seeding is kind-agnostic (no reachability regression, verified). 100% cov (entrypoints.py 616/0), 15617 tests pass, schema+spec §13 updated. Secondary confidence-drift note (0.85 spec vs ~0.96 observed) left to WI-suvil family per the filing."  # dcbe
